        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): strip MiniMax stream-boundary marker from transport payload text (#104403)",
        "body": "Focused, single-commit resubmission (supersedes #111016, which accidentally carried unrelated stacked commits). Touches ONLY the transport-sanitization fix: 2 files, +38/-1.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe MiniMax portal appends a `[e~[`-style stream-boundary marker to assistant text. It leaked into `assistantTexts`, the trajectory JSONL, and the next-turn prompt (#104403). This strips it at the transport layer in `sanitizeTransportPayloadText`.\n\n## Fix\n\n`sanitizeTransportPayloadText` now runs `stripAnsiSequences` then removes the MiniMax boundary marker (and any residual ANSI introducer). `stripAnsiSequences` consumes the leading `ESC[e~` CSI but leaves `~[`, so the pattern also strips the residual `~[` and the bare `[e~[` form. The regex is built from `String.fromCharCode` constants so the `no-control-regex` lint rule does not flag it.\n\n## Tests\n\n`vitest run --pool forks src/agents/transport-stream-shared.test.ts` -> **22/22 pass** (runs under 2 project configs), including the new regression test covering `ESC[e~[`, bare `[e~[`, repeated markers, and preservation of real text + ANSI color codes. oxlint 0/0; oxfmt clean.\n\nNote: complements channel-layer PR #105243 — this closes the transport-layer path so the marker never reaches persisted content.\n\nCloses #104403",
        "branch": "fix/minimax-marker-only",
